netlab (2.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Native device-name resolution, no nmap and no root. Discovery now names
    the hosts in the neighbour table over a plain socket before (and even
    without) the elevated nmap scan: reverse DNS first -- which is how the
    gateway and other DHCP clients get a name -- then a NetBIOS node-status
    query for Windows, Samba, NAS boxes and printers. Names show up fast and
    without a password prompt; the nmap pass still follows for UPnP/mDNS.
