netlab (2.18.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes for the six findings of the 2.17.1 external audit.
  * The captured-packet counter no longer drops to the analysed total when a
    live capture is stopped -- a stopped capture keeps reporting what the
    reader actually captured, and only a loaded file uses the analysed count.
  * Live Traffic's Domain column is now filterable: host:/sni:/service: match
    the domain shown for a row, so a visible site is never hidden by its own
    filter.
  * A remote IP with several observed names is shown as "name +N", not a
    single certain site, since none of the names is tied to that flow; the
    per-flow service is still preferred when known, and every candidate name
    still matches the filter.
  * Clicking a mode or page tab that is already selected now navigates to it,
    so returning from a drill-down page (Selected Device, PCAP viewer,
    Settings) to the host list works in one click.
  * Offline, the Selected Device page judges "active" against the capture's
    own last timestamp, like the topology does, instead of the wall clock, so
    the two pages agree when reading an old pcap.
  * The About box now describes both halves -- passive analysis and the active
    interception modules -- instead of claiming there is no active side.

