netlab (2.16.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reliability pass on the interception path.
  * Helper: a session lock closes an arm/disarm race. Commands each run on
    their own thread, so two arms (or an arm racing a disarm) could corrupt
    the single session; the slot is now claimed under a lock before arming,
    so a second arm is refused rather than starting a parallel poisoning.
  * Arm: a wide scope resolved each target's MAC one blocking request at a
    time -- up to a second per host, minutes for a /24. It is now one batched
    ARP sweep (arp.resolve_many) that returns as soon as every host answers.
  * Frame-level proof of the flagship: the poisoner is tested against a fake
    socket for the exact forged frames in both directions and the healing
    frames on restore, so the poison logic is covered without a live datapath.
    validation/DATAPATH-VERIFICATION.md records what is and is not automatable
    here and the one command that proves the full path on real hardware.
  * Tooling: pytest-cov wired into the test extra (70% of testable logic);
    a GitHub Actions CI workflow runs the suite offscreen on every push.

 -- Erwin <thestrak118@gmail.com>  Wed, 24 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0500

