netlab (2.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NTLM relay over SMB2. A captured SMB/NTLM authentication is relayed live
    to an in-scope server instead of being cracked offline, so the target
    authenticates the operator to that server. Implemented from the wire up
    (NetBIOS, SMB2 NEGOTIATE/SESSION_SETUP, SPNEGO/NTLMSSP ferry) with no
    runtime dependency on impacket; the codec and a full end-to-end relay are
    tested against a real impacket SMB server and client over loopback.
  * New "NTLM relay" module on the Interception page with a "Relay target"
    field; the relay listens on redirected tcp/445 and is gated on the
    engagement scope (the relay target must be in scope) and audited.
  * NetLab does not defeat SMB signing, MIC or channel binding: a hardened
    server simply rejects the relayed authentication, and that is reported.

